{
  "html": [
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "h2",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Why CPU monitoring is important?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "p",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "I work at "
        },
        {
          "kind": "element",
          "name": "a",
          "attributes": [
            [
              "href",
              "http://voodoo.io/"
            ]
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": "Voodoo"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": ", a French company that creates mobile video games. We have a lot of challenges with performance, availability, and scalability because of the insane amount of traffic our infrastructure supports (billions of events/requests per day). In this setting, every metric is important and gives us a lot of information about the state of our system."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "p",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "When working with Node.js one of the most critical resources to monitor is the CPU. Most of the time, when working on a low traffic API or project we don't realize how many simple lines of code can have a huge impact on CPU. On the other hand, when traffic increases, a simple mistake can cost dearly."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "p",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "For memory, constant monitoring is the best practice to track the worst developer nightmare a.k.a memory leak."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "img",
      "attributes": [
        [
          "src",
          "https://miro.medium.com/max/60/1*5o3M5niyi911waUrKWVZ0Q.png?q=20"
        ]
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "p",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Memory leak in action"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "blockquote",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "element",
          "name": "p",
          "attributes": [],
          "children": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": "Stay focused on the CPU!"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "img",
      "attributes": [
        [
          "src",
          "https://miro.medium.com/max/60/1*8uOdeOfnUzTaFIY1r7oAMg.png?q=20"
        ]
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "p",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Basic CPU monitoring"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "h2",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "CPU profiling: what's the difference with CPU monitoring?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "p",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Basically, for Node.js, CPU profiling is nothing more than collecting data about functions which are CPU consuming."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "h2",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Add arguments to Node.js"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "p",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Node.js provides a way to collect data about CPU with two command lines."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "block": true,
      "language": "",
      "text": "node --prof app.js"
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "img",
      "attributes": [
        [
          "src",
          "https://miro.medium.com/max/60/1*e7gjTlzi55udTXbbPeEs2A.png?q=20"
        ]
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "p",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Output of — prof"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "ul",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "element",
          "name": "li",
          "attributes": [],
          "children": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": "It needs to restart the application to launch a CPU profiling"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "element",
          "name": "li",
          "attributes": [],
          "children": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": "It is NOT suited for a production environment"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "img",
      "attributes": [
        [
          "alt",
          "CPU profiling before optimization"
        ],
        [
          "src",
          "https://miro.medium.com/max/60/1*CANkRN_yzl9tfrGd2F41wQ.png?q=20"
        ]
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "p",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "CPU profiling before optimization"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "p",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "element",
          "name": "strong",
          "attributes": [],
          "children": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": "How can we identify an issue?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "p",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "A CPU profiling should be read like this: The wider is the block the more it consumes CPU. So we are looking for the widest blocks."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "img",
      "attributes": [
        [
          "alt",
          "CPU profiling after optimization"
        ],
        [
          "src",
          "https://miro.medium.com/max/60/1*EO-pr4RolgcAOj_Uk1rpDA.png?q=20"
        ]
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "p",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "CPU profiling after optimization"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "p",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "What do we observe? Blocks are a lot smaller! It means that functions consume less CPU individually."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "h2",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Conclusion"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "p",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "CPU profiling is a must-have for every Node.js application running on production."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
